// Donchian Breakout
//
// Buy when price closes above the highest high of the last N bars; leave when it closes
// below the lowest low of a shorter window. Richard Donchian's channel, and the core of
// the Turtle Traders' published rules — a technique documented for decades, implemented
// here from its description.
//
// It is a TREND system: it loses small and often, and pays for that with rare large wins.
// Judged on win rate it looks terrible. Judged on expectancy it is the reason trend
// following survived fifty years.
strategy("Donchian Breakout", overlay = true)

[upper, mid, lower] = donchian(20)
[xUp, xMid, xLow]   = donchian(10)

plot(upper, title = "Upper", color = color.mute)
plot(lower, title = "Lower", color = color.mute)

// `upper[1]` is the channel BEFORE this bar — comparing against `upper` would compare the
// high to a channel that already contains it, and nothing would ever break out.
if close > upper[1]
    strategy.entry("breakout", strategy.long)

if close < xLow[1]
    strategy.close("breakout")
